@startuml iam_c4_context
title IAM C4 - Level 1: System Context
caption Current behavior checked against source, migrations, and tests on 2026-08-14.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #334155
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #7C3AED
  BackgroundColor #EDE9FE
}

rectangle "School admin\nManages school users" as schoolAdmin <<Person>> #E0F2FE
rectangle "Teacher\nUses protected APIs" as teacher <<Person>> #E0F2FE
rectangle "Student or parent\nUses my endpoints" as studentParent <<Person>> #E0F2FE
rectangle "Mobile app user\nAuthenticates by JWT" as mobileUser <<Person>> #E0F2FE
rectangle "Bale bot / webhook\nLinked user lookup" as bale <<External>> #FEF3C7

rectangle "Roshdeandishe school management system\nSpring Boot modular monolith\nIAM owns identity and access" as system <<System>> #DCFCE7

database "PostgreSQL\nIAM schema tables" as postgres
rectangle "SMTP server\nActivation emails" as smtp <<External>> #FEF3C7
rectangle "SMS provider\nOTP delivery\n<b>NOT IMPLEMENTED</b>" as sms <<External>> #FEF3C7

schoolAdmin --> system : Browser session login\nschool admin APIs
teacher --> system : Browser session login\nprotected APIs
studentParent --> system : Browser session login\nmy endpoints
mobileUser --> system : JWT bearer token
bale --> system : Webhook

system --> postgres : IAM users, roles,\nmemberships, permissions,\nentitlements
system --> smtp : Activation email\nbest effort
system ..> sms : OTP delivery\n<b>stub, no provider is called</b>

legend right
  This is C4-style without external C4-PlantUML includes.
  It should render with the standard IntelliJ PlantUML plugin.

  The dashed SMS edge is an unimplemented stub, not current behavior.
  SmsDriver.sendOtp calls no provider: it can log the code in dev and
  otherwise fails closed, so setting an api-key does not enable delivery.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml iam_c4_containers
title IAM C4 - Level 2: Containers
caption Runtime containers involved in IAM authentication and authorization.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #334155
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #7C3AED
  BackgroundColor #EDE9FE
}

rectangle "Web browser\nJTE pages + Alpine fetch\nCookie session + CSRF token" as browser <<Client>> #DBEAFE
rectangle "Android app\nMobile client shell\nBearer token auth" as android <<Client>> #DBEAFE

rectangle "Spring Boot backend\nJava 21 modular monolith\nIAM, school, academic, finance, ...\nSession and JWT authentication\nAspect-based authorization" as backend <<Container>> #DCFCE7

database "PostgreSQL\nFlyway-managed schemas" as db
rectangle "SMTP\nActivation emails" as mail <<External>> #FEF3C7
rectangle "SMS gateway\nOTP delivery\n<b>NOT IMPLEMENTED</b>" as sms <<External>> #FEF3C7

browser --> backend : HTML + JSON APIs\nX-School-ID on protected APIs
android --> backend : POST /api/auth/token\nAuthorization: Bearer

backend --> db : JPA repositories
backend --> mail : JavaMailSender
backend ..> sms : SmsDriver\n<b>stub, no provider is called</b>

note bottom of backend
Authorization is not based on Spring Security authorities.
Protected school APIs use @RequiresModule and @RequiresPermission
backed by IAM tables.

The dashed SMS edge is an unimplemented stub. SmsDriver.sendOtp calls
no provider: it can log the code in dev and otherwise fails closed, so
OTP login cannot be enabled by configuration alone.
end note
@enduml

@startuml iam_c4_components
title IAM C4 - Level 3: IAM Components
caption Controllers, security aspects, facade, services, and persistence tables.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #334155
  RoundCorner 10
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #7C3AED
  BackgroundColor #EDE9FE
}

package "IAM HTTP entry points" as http {
  rectangle "AuthController" as auth #DBEAFE
  rectangle "MeController" as me #DBEAFE
  rectangle "MembershipController" as membershipController #DBEAFE
  rectangle "RoleController" as roleController #DBEAFE
  rectangle "Login/Register/Activate\npage controllers" as pageControllers #DBEAFE
}

package "Authentication and request security" as security {
  rectangle "SecurityConfig" as securityConfig #E0F2FE
  rectangle "IamUserDetailsService" as userDetails #E0F2FE
  rectangle "JwtTokenProvider" as jwtProvider #E0F2FE
  rectangle "JwtAuthenticationFilter" as jwtFilter #E0F2FE
  rectangle "ModuleAccessAspect" as moduleAspect #E0F2FE
  rectangle "PermissionAccessAspect" as permissionAspect #E0F2FE
}

package "Platform module (outside IAM)" as platformPkg {
  rectangle "TenantResolverFilter" as tenantFilter #FEF3C7
  rectangle "TenantContext\nThreadLocal" as tenantContext #FEF3C7
}

package "IAM public API" as publicApi {
  interface "IamFacade" as facade
  rectangle "AccessContext\nAccessDecision" as accessTypes #DBEAFE
}

package "IAM application services" as app {
  rectangle "IamFacadeImpl" as facadeImpl #DCFCE7
  rectangle "AccessDecisionService" as accessDecision #DCFCE7
  rectangle "PermissionDecisionService" as permissionDecision #DCFCE7
  rectangle "InviteEmailSender" as inviteSender #DCFCE7
  rectangle "SmsDriver\n<b>no provider call yet</b>" as smsDriver #DCFCE7
  rectangle "IamSeedDataRunner" as seedRunner #DCFCE7
}

package "IAM persistence" as persistence {
  database "iam.users" as users
  database "iam.school_memberships" as memberships
  database "iam.roles" as roles
  database "iam.permissions" as permissions
  database "iam.role_permissions" as rolePermissions
  database "iam.modules" as modules
  database "iam.school_entitlements" as schoolEntitlements
  database "iam.user_entitlements" as userEntitlements
  database "iam.invite_tokens" as inviteTokens
  database "iam.verification_codes" as verificationCodes
}

auth --> facade : calls
me --> facade : calls
membershipController --> facade : calls
roleController --> facade : calls
pageControllers ..> auth : renders pages for

securityConfig --> userDetails : configures
securityConfig --> jwtFilter : installs
jwtFilter --> jwtProvider : validates JWT
moduleAspect --> facade : checkAccess
permissionAspect --> facade : checkPermission
tenantFilter --> tenantContext : sets per request
moduleAspect --> tenantContext : reads
permissionAspect --> tenantContext : reads

facade <|.. facadeImpl
facadeImpl --> accessDecision
facadeImpl --> permissionDecision
facadeImpl --> inviteSender
facadeImpl --> smsDriver

userDetails --> users : reads
facadeImpl --> users : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> memberships : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> roles : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> permissions : reads
facadeImpl --> rolePermissions : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> modules : reads
facadeImpl --> schoolEntitlements : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> inviteTokens : reads/writes
facadeImpl --> verificationCodes : reads/writes

accessDecision --> modules : reads
accessDecision --> schoolEntitlements : SCHOOL scope
accessDecision --> userEntitlements : USER scope
permissionDecision --> memberships : active memberships
permissionDecision --> permissions : required permission
permissionDecision --> rolePermissions : role grants

seedRunner --> modules : seed catalog
seedRunner --> roles : seed system roles
seedRunner --> permissions : seed catalog
seedRunner --> rolePermissions : seed grants

note bottom
Spring Security establishes identity only.
IAM aspects enforce module entitlement and permission using active
memberships and role-permission rows.

IamFacadeImpl calls SmsDriver, but SmsDriver.sendOtp reaches no SMS
provider yet. AccessDecisionService reads modules and the two
entitlement tables only; role rows are read through IamFacadeImpl.
end note
@enduml

@startuml iam_c4_password_login
title IAM Flow - Password Login

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor User
participant AuthController
participant AuthenticationManager
participant IamUserDetailsService
database "iam.users" as Users
participant HttpSession

User -> AuthController : POST /api/auth/login
AuthController -> AuthenticationManager : authenticate(email, password)
AuthenticationManager -> IamUserDetailsService : loadUserByUsername(email)
IamUserDetailsService -> Users : findByEmail(email)
Users --> IamUserDetailsService : user with password_hash
AuthenticationManager --> AuthController : Authentication
AuthController -> HttpSession : save SecurityContext
AuthController --> User : LoginResponse(email)
@enduml

@startuml iam_c4_school_scoped_authorization
title IAM Flow - School-Scoped Authorization

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Client
participant TenantResolverFilter
participant ModuleAccessAspect
participant PermissionAccessAspect
participant IamFacade
participant AccessDecisionService
participant PermissionDecisionService
participant Controller

Client -> TenantResolverFilter : API request with X-School-ID
TenantResolverFilter -> TenantResolverFilter : set TenantContext
note over ModuleAccessAspect, PermissionAccessAspect
@RequiresModule and @RequiresPermission are independent.
A method may carry either, both, or neither; each aspect
reads TenantContext itself. Both shown here for completeness.
end note
ModuleAccessAspect -> IamFacade : checkAccess(user, module, school)
IamFacade -> AccessDecisionService : decide(...)
AccessDecisionService --> ModuleAccessAspect : granted or denied
PermissionAccessAspect -> IamFacade : checkPermission(user, permission, school)
IamFacade -> PermissionDecisionService : decide(...)
PermissionDecisionService --> PermissionAccessAspect : granted or denied
PermissionAccessAspect -> Controller : proceed if granted
Controller -> Controller : TenantContext.requireMatches(path schoolId)
@enduml

@startuml iam_c4_member_invite_activation
title IAM Flow - Add Member And Activate Account

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Admin
participant MembershipController
participant IamFacadeImpl
database "iam.users" as Users
database "iam.school_memberships" as Memberships
database "iam.invite_tokens" as Invites
participant SMTP
actor Invitee
participant AuthController

Admin -> MembershipController : POST /memberships
MembershipController -> IamFacadeImpl : findOrCreateUser(email, fullName)
IamFacadeImpl -> Users : create or reuse user
MembershipController -> IamFacadeImpl : createMembership(userId, schoolId, roleCode)
IamFacadeImpl -> Memberships : create or reactivate row

Admin -> MembershipController : POST /{membershipId}/invite-token
MembershipController -> IamFacadeImpl : issueInviteToken(schoolId, membershipId)
IamFacadeImpl -> Invites : reuse valid token or create new one
IamFacadeImpl -> SMTP : send activation link best effort

Invitee -> AuthController : POST /api/auth/activate
AuthController -> IamFacadeImpl : redeemInviteToken(token, newPassword)
IamFacadeImpl -> Users : set password_hash
IamFacadeImpl -> Invites : set redeemed_at
@enduml
